libc++ requires std::unique_ptr<T>'s default deleter to see a complete T at
destructor instantiation time.  lld 21 has a few ELF classes with inline
implicit destructors that own forward-declared types, which libstdc++ accepts
in this build but libc++ rejects.  Move those destructors out-of-line into
translation units that already include the complete definitions.

